  "diagnosis": {
    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 1.03,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.08,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings plateau at about 0.97-1.0 from 6 h onward. I tested whether that plateau was reader saturation by diluting the 18 h aliquot. Scaled back by the dilution factor, the results were: 10x gave 0.1064, or about 1.06 (replicates 0.1071 and 0.1056); 3x gave 0.327, or about 0.98; 50x gave 0.0186, or about 0.93 (noisy, replicates 0.0225 and 0.0148). All sit within about 10% of the undiluted 0.97. If the reader were saturating or hiding biomass, the diluted readings scaled up would be well above the undiluted value, and they are not. The culture therefore appears to have a true stationary plateau at OD of roughly 1.0, with at most slight nonlinearity."
  },
